    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\"><span class=\"learn-keyword\">Animal improvement</span> involves the deliberate application of breeding techniques to enhance the productivity, quality and desirable characteristics of livestock.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning and Objectives of Animal Improvement</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Animal improvement aims to increase productivity (milk, meat, eggs, wool), improve disease resistance, enhance growth rate and feed efficiency, and develop breeds suited to local environmental conditions.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Methods of Animal Improvement</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Inbreeding</td><td>Mating of closely related animals to fix and concentrate desirable genetic traits within a breed</td></tr><tr><td>Crossbreeding</td><td>Mating animals of different breeds to combine desirable traits from each (hybrid vigour)</td></tr><tr><td>Artificial insemination (AI)</td><td>Collecting semen from a selected male and introducing it into the female's reproductive tract without natural mating</td></tr><tr><td>Embryo transfer</td><td>Transferring a fertilised embryo from a genetically superior donor female into a surrogate female to carry the pregnancy</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Advantages of Animal Improvement</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Increases productivity (meat, milk, eggs) and farmer income.</li><li>Allows rapid, controlled spread of desirable genetics (especially via AI and embryo transfer).</li><li>Reduces the risk and cost of transporting breeding males over long distances.</li><li>Can introduce disease resistance and better adaptation to local conditions.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Limitations of Animal Improvement</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Inbreeding, if excessive, can increase the risk of genetic defects and reduced fertility.</li><li>Requires skilled technicians and specialised equipment, especially for AI and embryo transfer.</li><li>Can be costly, particularly for embryo transfer technology.</li><li>Crossbred animals may not always breed true in subsequent generations.</li></ul><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Remember that inbreeding fixes traits WITHIN a breed, while crossbreeding combines traits BETWEEN different breeds — this distinction is frequently examined.</div>",
